r than me  i'm gonna go coach high school football  you guys run the company and they did a  great job i always tell everybody i  worked hard my whole life to getting  back to doing what i love the most  when i first started coaching it was  like herding cats if you're if you want  to be competitive in  you know  high level california football  that it's it's 12 months of the year now  you know we we end our season we're in  the weight room the following monday  and a parent stood up and said why are  you doing this i said because it's hard  because boys need hard  because life is hard  my first season we were six and four in  18 we were  12 and  we've won the toughest league in the  county three times the expectations are  high  in march 2020 before our spring break  we were told school would be closed for  two weeks  it ended up being for over a year  i got more phone calls from kids in  trouble  from march of 2020 to  march of 2021  in all of my previous 14 years combined  we were right there  our kids after a lift i was looking at  the kids  and i i don't even know what came over  me but i looked at the kids i say look  i'm probably  going to crash and burn  but i promise you  i'm gonna do everything i can  as your head coach to get sports back  and that's how it started  local coaches parents and athletes say  enough is enough it's time for change  it's time to play sports again and now  they're holding an event to get the  state to pay attention head football  coach at torrey pines high school ron  gladden ron gladnick ron gladnick coach  thank you for once again joining us we  started we we formed six seal teams of  parent volunteers who had different jobs  i was in charge of seal team six  which was engaging our politicians we  started an app and we got 1600 head high  school football coaches in california in  the app and 7 000 assistant coaches  so 11 days after i started it was 4 30  in the afternoon my cell phone rang and  it was gavin newsom  talked  for 45 minutes and what i left him with  was this  i said governor we are not political we  do not want to be political we want to  do the right thing for kids  he wanted sports back but the  mosh pit of special interests that you  had to work through to get it back  from that day took five weeks until we  finally got it  done  and as a result not only did we get high  school football back we got all high  school sports back  all seasons were played from march to  june  youth sports were returned  it was incredible  three mil 3.3 million kids got to play  what could be better than that  at the end of the day our our whole  program here has nothing to do with  football  it has everything to do with building  great young men  and i believe if you do that the  football will take care of itself  and i learned that from dick lowry this  is stuff i learned from my college head  coach my defensive coordinator  so you know for me it all started there  [Music]
 

